Looking at this code, `nextClearBit` returns the index of the first bit set to `false` at or after `fromIndex`. So every bit from `fromIndex` up to (but excluding) the returned index `\result` must be set (`true`). "fromIndex is valid" means `fromIndex >= 0`.

<code>assert fromIndex >= 0 => \forall int i; fromIndex <= i && i < \result; this.get(i);</code>
